1. CSC 411 course starter code

   Problem Set 03 starter code by Professor Adam Gaweda, CSC 411, North Carolina State
   University. Used with the instructor's permission. This includes:

     src/edu/ncsu/csc411/ps03/environment/
     src/edu/ncsu/csc411/ps03/utils/
     src/edu/ncsu/csc411/ps03/agent/ConfigurationSolver.java (template)
     inputs/public/

2. City of Raleigh Open Data

   Fire incidents (Fire Incidents, Fire Incidents Past Month) and city limits
   (Corporate Limits Dissolved), used under the Open Raleigh data policy:
   https://data.raleighnc.gov/

   The City of Raleigh makes no warranty as to the accuracy or completeness of
   its data and may ask that use of it stop. Files derived from it:

     inputs/raleigh/scenarios/
     inputs/raleigh/raleigh_outline.csv
     inputs/raleigh/travel_model.properties
     test/resources/raleigh_*.json

3. Wake County Open Data

   Fire station locations (FireStations), licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Source: https://data-wake.opendata.arcgis.com/

   File derived from it: inputs/raleigh/stations.csv

This project is a teaching model, not a dispatch tool. Neither the City of
Raleigh nor Wake County endorses it.
